# Agent instructions for this workspace

## Always operate under /workspace

Your `cwd` for shell/file tools is `/workspace` — this directory. Do not
write session output, downloads, or generated files anywhere outside it
(not the container's own `$HOME`, not `/tmp`). See
`HERMES_DOCKER_SANDBOX_REFERENCE.md` in this same directory for the full
reasoning (checkpointing and persistence only cover `/workspace`).

## When you're genuinely stuck, delegate — don't keep guessing

`delegate_task` is now pinned to a frontier model
(`delegation.provider: anthropic`, `delegation.model: claude-sonnet-4-6`
in `~/.hermes/config.yaml`) — a delegated subagent is a real second
opinion, not just another copy of yourself.

**Use `delegate_task` proactively, without waiting to be told, when you
notice any of these:**
- You've retried the same class of fix 2+ times and it's still failing
  (e.g. the same category of syntax error, the same wrong assumption
  about how something works).
- You're about to guess at an API, a language feature, or a system
  behavior you're not confident about, instead of verifying it.
- A `/goal`-mode judge (or the user) has told you your last attempt was
  blocked or unsatisfactory for the same underlying reason twice.

Give the delegated subagent a **self-contained** goal — it knows nothing
of this conversation. Include the exact error text, what you already
tried, and the specific question you need answered. Don't delegate
mechanical work with no reasoning involved (`execute_code` is cheaper
and faster for that) — this is for the cases where you're actually
stuck, not busywork.

Full writeup of why this is set up this way:
https://github.com/danindiana/hermes-gpu-docker-architecture/tree/master/delegate-to-frontier
